     7	measured Governance Decay failure (§2.2 of PLAN-179) is not "the model
     8	forgot WHERE the rules live", it is "the rules themselves were summarized
     9	away and the model then violated them". The mitigation is to quarantine a
    10	SMALL, CLOSED set of invariants from the lossy compression and re-state
    11	them verbatim after every compaction.
    12	
    13	## Amendment r1-C5 — the set is a CODE CONSTANT, never disk-sourced
    14	
    15	``PINNED_CONSTRAINTS`` is a literal tuple in this module. It is **never**
    16	loaded from a ``.md`` (or any other file) at runtime. That is not a style
    17	preference — it is what makes two claims TRUE by construction:
    18	
    19	1. *"Not derived from disk"* — there is no file read on this path, so
    20	   there is no window in which a compacted/edited/replaced document can
    21	   change what the model is told the rules are.
    22	2. *"Immune to Compaction-Eviction"* — the constant lives in code that is
    23	   re-executed per hook invocation, outside the transcript the summarizer
    24	   rewrites.
    25	
    26	This module therefore performs **no file I/O whatsoever** — that property
    27	is asserted by a test that scans this source. Changing the pinned set is a
    28	canonical edit of ``.claude/hooks/_lib/`` and requires the Owner-signed
    29	sentinel ceremony (ADR-031), which is exactly the friction the set
    30	deserves.
