.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md:502:| `ledger_checkpoint_recorded` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `outcome` (str — CLOSED enum: `ledger_updated` / `ledger_missing` / `ledger_absent_from_plan` / `error` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape via the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator, else `unknown`; a path-traversal attempt smuggled through this field is rejected, not echoed), `scope_source` (str — CLOSED enum: `plan_dir` / `plan_ac` / `both` / `other`; how the commit was found to be in scope), `in_scope_path_count` (int 0..99 — clamped), `ledger_size_bucket_kib` (int 0..99 — clamped KiB bucket; the unit is in the field NAME), `over_ceiling` (int 0/1), `unverified_ac_claim_count` (int 0..99 — ledger bullets naming an AC/US id with no `verifier:` clause), `commits_since_last_observation` (int 0..99 — clamped), `state_kind` (str — CLOSED enum: `fresh` / `resumed` / `unavailable`; off-enum COERCED to `unavailable`), `would_block` (int 0/1 — what the FUTURE enforce flip WOULD have done; the hook has no deny path today), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W2 US6 / ADR-195 — the work-boundary ledger checkpoint, ADVISORY by construction (`check_ledger_checkpoint.py`, PreToolUse/Bash; no branch in that module returns `permissionDecision`). EVERY int is TYPE-strict: `bool` is rejected as an `int` subclass and a `float` becomes `0` rather than being rounded, because `_lib/canonical_json.py` refuses floats in HMAC-covered fields and the spool writer would drop the ENTIRE event to an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb (S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the commit MESSAGE, the committed PATHS, the ledger CONTENT, the repo root, any AC text. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md-503-| `ledger_checkpoint_skipped` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `reason` (str — CLOSED enum: `out_of_scope_paths` / `kill_switch` / `hotfix` / `exploratory` / `operator_opt_out` / `unparseable` / `budget_exhausted` / `no_repo` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed — the reason is an ENUM and never free text, so "why the rail stayed quiet" is countable without ever describing the commit), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN`, else `unknown`), `commits_since_last_observation` (int 0..99 — clamped), `state_kind` (str — CLOSED enum: `fresh` / `resumed` / `unavailable`), `would_block` (int 0/1 — always `0` on this row: a skip is never a would-block), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W2 US6 / ADR-195 — the same rail's NEGATIVE case, a separate action on purpose: the measure-first window needs a DENOMINATOR, and "skipped because the commit touched no plan-scoped path" and "never observed at all" are different facts that absence alone cannot distinguish. `reason=kill_switch` is emitted even when `CEO_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT=0`, so "the rail is off" is itself measured; `CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1` is the one fully silent posture (master precedence, CLAUDE.md §4). Same TYPE-strict int discipline as the row above. Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIPPED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. NO ATLAS technique. |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md-504-| `ledger_entry_rejected` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `signal` (str — fixed vocabulary of ONE: `ledger_write_gate`; this action has exactly one producer, so any other value names a caller that is not the gate and is COERCED), `decision` (str — CLOSED enum: `accept` / `reject`; an unreadable value COERCES to `reject`, FAIL-CLOSED, because an unreadable security verdict is a rejection and never an acceptance), `reason` (str — CLOSED enum: `ok` / `not_scanned_trusted_provenance` / `scanner_hit` / `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input`; off-enum COERCES to `malformed_input`, also fail-CLOSED), `family` (str — CLOSED enum, the UNION of the gate's own local families {`none`, `scanner_unavailable`, `oversize`, `malformed_input`, `unknown_family`} and the pattern CATALOGUE `_lib/injection_patterns.family_names()` {`directive_prose`, `harness_mimicry`, `provider_tokens`, `role_preamble`}; off-enum COERCED to `unknown_family`. Deliberately STRICTER than `prompt_injection_detected`, whose branch allowlists `family` by NAME but leaves its VALUE caller-chosen), `hits_count` (int 0..9999 — clamped), `bytes_scanned` (int 0..8192 — clamped at the gate's `MAX_ENTRY_BYTES`; an oversize body is rejected WITHOUT scanning, so this ceiling can never truncate a legitimate value), `scanned` (int 0/1), `enforced` (int 0/1 — whether the fail-CLOSED verdict BINDS in the current posture; kept separate from `decision` so an advisory-window row records what enforcement WOULD have done without pretending it happened), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W4 / ADR-195 — the ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), registered by Owner decision 2026-08-25 ("3 actions"). It exists precisely so a discard is NOT filed as `prompt_injection_detected`: routing `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input` into a DETECTION action would poison the very false-positive series the advisory window has to measure. There is deliberately NO fallback action — a missing or raising emitter degrades to a LOUD breadcrumb and `audit_channel="unavailable"`, never to a quieter series. Typed emitter `emit_ledger_entry_rejected` (keywords mirror `GateVerdict.to_audit_fields()` exactly). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the rejected entry BODY (not even a truncated preview — public repo, LLM06), the entry id, and any path. NO ATLAS technique (the DETECTION that may underlie a `scanner_hit` is `prompt_injection_detected`'s job; this row is the gate's disposal record). |
