.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md:530:| `compaction_context_reinjected` (v2.43) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape, else `unknown`), `snapshot_found` (bool — coerced to `false`), `snapshot_age_s` (int — clamped 0..9999999), `pointer_count` (int — clamped 0..9; POINTERS ONLY. Its meaning is UNCHANGED by PLAN-179, deliberately: a counter that is silently re-scoped makes its own historical series uncomparable, so the constraint block below got a NEW counter instead of a widened one. A consumer may compare `pointer_count` across the whole v2.43+ series), `constraint_count` (int — v2.56 / PLAN-179 W1-b, amendment r1-C3: the count of PINNED GOVERNANCE CONSTRAINTS re-stated verbatim after compaction, sourced from `_lib/pinned_constraints.constraint_count()` — the SET size, never the rendered LINE count, because the block carries a header line and a counter that drifts with formatting is not a counter. Constraints and pointers hold SEPARATE budgets: the 9-line pointer cap can never truncate a governance rule. Treatment in the scrub branch: `max(0, min(99, int(...)))` with the same `except (TypeError, ValueError) -> 0` fallback the sibling counters use. **STATUS — both halves land in THIS ceremony (PLAN-179 W0/W1):** `constraint_count` IS a member of `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST` and the `compaction_context_reinjected` dispatch branch carries the clamp above, so the deny-by-default scrub KEEPS the field and `check_postcompact_reinject.py` puts a real clamped `int` on the wire. A consumer MUST still read an ABSENT `constraint_count` as “this producer predates constraint pinning”, NEVER as “zero constraints pinned” — absence and zero are different facts, and `constraint_count=0` is itself meaningful (it is what `CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0` produces)), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-135 W2 H1 (anthropic-surface-harvest; ADR-153 compaction-continuity) — PostCompact governance reinjection: after compaction, `check_postcompact_reinject.py` read the PreCompact snapshot from the plan scratchpad and reinjected governance POINTERS (active PLAN, execution-unit position, Gate-1 re-read reminder, pending ceremonies, HMAC anchor) via `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. POINTERS ONLY — never file CONTENTS (the Option-A prompt-injection surface, ADR-153 §Decision). ONE emit per PostCompact event. Producer: `.claude/hooks/check_postcompact_reinject.py` via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_REINJECTED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the reinjected pointer TEXT, the plan path/label, the ceremony paths, the scratchpad body (only the closed enums + counters persist). PLAN-179 W1-b [r1-C3] prepends a PINNED GOVERNANCE CONSTRAINT block AHEAD of the pointers: a pointer is not a restriction — ADR-153's pointers say WHERE the rules live, the pinned block re-states the rules THEMSELVES from a CODE constant (`_lib/pinned_constraints.PINNED_CONSTRAINTS`), never from disk, so the prompt-injection reasoning that forces POINTERS-ONLY on the snapshot simply does not apply to it. The constraint TEXT is no more on the wire than the pointer text — only `constraint_count` is. Dedicated kill-switch `CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0`, deliberately SEPARATE from `CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY=0`: an operator disarming the continuity SNAPSHOT must not silently disarm the governance floor. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
