_PAIR_RAIL_HUMAN_TRIAGE_HOURS env override), `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6: the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget this invocation ran under, in integer MILLISECONDS, NOT float seconds; canonical_json no-float invariant, same encoding as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` — divide by 1000 to recover seconds; off-shape/NaN/inf/bool COERCED to 0 = "unknown budget", bounded in the typed wrapper AND re-coerced in the `emit_generic` dispatch branch. Purpose is §4(i): before this field a case F produced by a sub-floor `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S` export was byte-INDISTINGUISHABLE from a genuine Codex outage, which made the undocumented knob stealthier than the documented kill-switch. Encoding is load-bearing, not stylistic: a float in an HMAC-covered field is rejected by `_lib/canonical_json.py` and the spool writer then DROPS THE WHOLE EVENT with only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb — for this action that would manufacture the very /ceo-boot liveness deficit `review_id` exists to disprove), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline HMAC-chain invariant. PLAN-081 Phase 3 (S100 ceremony 2026-05-10) — emitted by `.claude/hooks/check_pair_rail.py:_decide_with_matrix()` once per Pair-Rail PreToolUse evaluation that reaches the matrix arm (write tool + L3+ path + no sentinel bypass). Source action for `fp_rate_30d` and `disagreement_rate_30d` predicate aggregators. ADR-107 + ADR-108 ACCEPTED gate. Sec MF-3 invariant: NEVER persist raw Codex review body / proposed-content / file path. Registered with `KERNEL_OVERRIDE` bypass since `audit_emit.py` is in `_KERNEL_PATHS`. |
