.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md-493-| `council_lane_invoked` (v2.51) | `action`, `vendor` (str — CLOSED enum: `claude` / `codex` / `grok` / `other`; coerced), `lane_status` (str — CLOSED enum: `ok` / `unavailable` / `other`; coerced), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-156 Wave 6 / ADR-162 (2026-07-12) — one append per AVAILABLE external council lane per `/council` run: the auditable record that repo scope LEFT the process to an external vendor (xAI/OpenAI). Typed emitter `emit_council_lane_invoked`; dedicated deny-by-default `_COUNCIL_LANE_INVOKED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + closed-enum coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the audited SCOPE text, findings, any prompt bytes — the row records the FACT of egress, never its content (the operator ratifies the egress at OQ5). **Completeness residual (named):** an absent row is not evidence of an absent invocation. NO ATLAS technique (governance/egress breadcrumb). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md-494-| `codex_review_verdict` (v2.52) | `action`, `outcome` (str — CLOSED enum: `clean` / `findings` / `skipped_failopen` / `detected_only`; an unrecognized value is COERCED to `skipped_failopen` — never to a healthy-class value, so unparseable telemetry input can never claim rail health), `diff_sha256` (str — 64-lowercase-hex sha256 of the reviewed assembled risky diff, shape-validated; any off-shape value COERCED to `""`), `session_id` (threaded from the Stop-hook stdin event, fallback `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` env, then `""`), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 (2026-07-27) — Stop-hook cross-model review OUTCOME, emitted by `codex_review_user_code.py` once per distinct (`diff_sha256`, `outcome`) pair (telemetry dedupe SEPARATE from the review-status dedupe, so Stop-retry loops re-review without re-emitting). `clean`/`findings` require a strictly PARSED verdict (bounded `- <file>: <issue>` grammar or exact `CLEAN`); infra fail-open (codex missing / rc!=0 / empty stdout / timeout) AND malformed output both map to `skipped_failopen`; DETECT-ONLY default mode maps its nudge to `detected_only` (neutral). Feeds the /ceo-boot `failopen_rail_liveness_7d` `stop_review` sub-rail. Typed emitter `emit_codex_review_verdict`; dedicated deny-by-default `_CODEX_REVIEW_VERDICT_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + VALUE re-coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the verdict TEXT, the diff content, file paths (a Codex finding can quote secrets from the reviewed diff). Deliberately NOT `pair_rail_codex_unavailable` — that action feeds the dispatcher's Codex-outage predicate and must stay unpolluted. NO ATLAS technique (liveness telemetry, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md-495-| `pair_rail_review_expected` (v2.52) | `action`, `tool_name` (str — CLOSED enum: `Edit` / `Write` / `MultiEdit` / `NotebookEdit` / `unknown`; off-enum COERCED to `unknown`), `file_path_hash_prefix` (str — 16-hex SHA-256 prefix of target file path, the SAME token/helper as `pair_rail_case`; bounded shape `[0-9a-f]{0,16}`, off-shape COERCED to empty; raw path forbidden per LLM06 side-channel guard; r4 F2, retained as the LEGACY fallback bucket key + harmless secondary key — id-less events still pair per (session, file-hash) BUCKET), `review_id` (str — exact-shape `([0-9a-f]{16})?` (EXACTLY 16 lowercase hex, or empty; r6 F2: raw value validated, off-shape incl. oversize DROPPED to empty — never truncated); r5 F2 — THE invocation correlation key: minted per review entry by `_decide()` (`os.urandom(8).hex()`) and identical on this emit and the same invocation's `pair_rail_case`, so the /ceo-boot deficit pairs a specific expected with its OWN case — counting (even (session, file-hash)-bucketed) cannot: an old completed case for the SAME (session, file) offset a later dead expected 1:1. An EXPECTED `review_id` with no matching `pair_rail_case` in-window = an outstanding (dead) review -> RED; off-shape COERCED to empty; empty falls back to the bucket-count heuristic (best-effort, pre-land events only — post-land every review carries an id)), `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6: the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget the paired review runs under, in integer MILLISECONDS, NOT float seconds; canonical_json no-float invariant, same encoding as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` — divide by 1000 to recover seconds; off-shape/NaN/inf/bool COERCED to 0 = "unknown budget", bounded in the typed wrapper AND re-coerced in the `emit_generic` dispatch branch. Carried on the DENOMINATOR as well as the case so the pair records the budget it ran under even when the case never arrives — see the `pair_rail_case` row for the §4(i) rationale and for why the integer encoding is load-bearing), `session_id` (explicit required kwarg on the typed emitter — the hook threads the PreToolUse event's own session id, no silent default), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 (2026-07-27) — canonical-edit review ENTERED marker, emitted by `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` only after the kill-switch / non-write-tool / not-L3+ / sentinel-bypass arms have all returned (those paths emit NOTHING). The durable session-correlated DENOMINATOR for the /ceo-boot `pair_rail` activity-conditioned liveness row: a window session with expected-but-no-outcome is the S254 dead-rail class and escalates RED; zero expected + zero outcomes is vacuously green; a healthy outcome from session B never masks session A. Typed emitter `emit_pair_rail_review_expected`; dedicated deny-by-default `_PAIR_RAIL_REVIEW_EXPECTED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + closed-enum coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: file paths, proposed content, any review text. NO ATLAS technique (liveness telemetry, not a detection signal). |
