.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md-499-| `context_pressure_observed` (v2.56) | `action`, `used_bucket` (int — CLOSED set of PERCENT rungs: `40` / `60` / `80` / `90` / `95`; the unit lives in the field NAME. The check `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` is TYPE-strict: `bool` is rejected (it is an `int` subclass, so `True` would otherwise sail through any numeric test) and `float` is rejected even when it COMPARES equal to a rung (`40.0 in {40}` is `True` in Python), because `_lib/canonical_json.py` refuses floats in HMAC-covered fields and the spool writer then drops the ENTIRE event, leaving only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb — the same S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2 class as `pair_rail_case.timeout_ms`. Anything off-set is COERCED to the sentinel `0`, deliberately OUTSIDE the enum so a consumer can always tell a real rung from a coerced one), `event_source` (str — CLOSED enum: `precompact` / `sessionstart_compact` / `userpromptsubmit` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed. Only `precompact` has a shipped producer in the PLAN-179 W0/W1 bundle; `sessionstart_compact` — the channel PLAN-179 debate amendment 8.1 designates PRIMARY — and `userpromptsubmit` are RESERVED, and a consumer MUST read their absence as “no producer yet”, NEVER as “no pressure observed on that channel”. The PostCompact `additionalContext` channel stays UNPROVEN until the PLAN-179 W0-1 probe lands and is therefore deliberately ABSENT from the enum), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape via the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator, else `unknown`), `session_id` (present ONLY when the producer holds a session id derived from the HOOK INPUT; deliberately OMITTED otherwise rather than filled from `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`, which an agent can set — an unattributed row is honest, a wrongly-attributed one is not; PLAN-179 amendment r1-C1), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W0 US2 / debate amendment 8.1 (ADR-153 continuity successor rail, 2026-08-18) — EDGE-TRIGGERED context-pressure breadcrumb: the session crossed INTO a new context-usage percent rung. A TRANSITION, never a per-turn sample — the hysteresis gate is `audit_emit.should_emit_context_pressure(used_bucket, state_dir)`, which persists the last rung in the marker `context-pressure-last-bucket` under the gitignored `.claude/state/` and FAILS OPEN (any state I/O error means “emit”: a bookkeeping file may never block or crash a user session, and fail-CLOSED here would silently lose the very signal PLAN-179 exists to measure). Without that gate the rail would append one row per prompt while the session sits in a single rung. Off-enum input never re-arms the marker — a bogus value must not be able to suppress the NEXT real transition. Emitted via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper — the `settings_tamper_detected` / compaction-pair precedent). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the raw token/byte counts, the exact percentage (a precise figure is a side channel on session size — the rung is the governance signal), the transcript text, the plan PATH text, the prompt body. NO ATLAS technique (governance/observability breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md-500-| `ceremony_lint_unlock_used` (v2.57) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `file_sha256` (str — 16-hex sha256 PREFIX of the unlocked ceremony script; shape-checked, anything malformed COERCED to the sentinel `"invalid"`, never echoed), `reason_len` (int — length of the mandatory `CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_REASON`; TYPE-strict like `used_bucket` — `bool` rejected as an `int` subclass, non-int rejected, then clamped 0..9999; a float on the wire would make `_lib/canonical_json.py` drop the WHOLE event to an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb, the S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2 class), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-174 W1 — the ceremony-lint ADR-186-pattern escape hatch of `check-ceremony-script.py` (`CEO_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK=<sha256>` + mandatory reason; unlock without a reason keeps the block). Producer: `.claude/scripts/check-ceremony-script.py::_emit_unlock_audit` via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper — the `settings_tamper_detected` precedent). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_CEREMONY_LINT_UNLOCK_USED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the unlock REASON text (stderr-only, operator-facing), the script path, the script body. Registration history: the emitter shipped in PLAN-174 W1 (`7d467a8`) WITHOUT this row, `check-audit-registry-coverage` correctly flagged the orphan (6 red jobs), the emit was PARKED in `908707e` ("um emissor nao embarca antes do registro dele") and is RESTORED by the same SENT-S318 pack that lands this row (`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 325 -> 326). NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md-501-| `salt_rotation_registered` (v2.58) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `reason` (str — CLOSED enum {`first_mint`, `migration_mint`, `other`}; anything else COERCED to `other`, never echoed), `salt_scope` (str — fixed vocabulary of one: `project`, the ADR-079 S318 salt unit; anything else COERCED), `slug_sha256` (str — 16-hex sha256 PREFIX of the native project slug; shape-checked, malformed COERCED to the sentinel `"invalid"`, never echoed), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-182 W1 — the ONE sanctioned, REGISTERED salt-rotation event (ADR-079 S318 amendment §2: minting a per-project `.salt` is observable in the chain, never silent; the pre-S318 `get_instance_salt()` minted with no error, no log, no signal). Producer: `_lib/injection_salt.py::_register_mint` via LAZY `emit_generic` at mint time only (no module-load coupling; a `salt-minted.json` sidecar next to the salt is the forensic ground truth when the emit path is unavailable). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_SALT_ROTATION_REGISTERED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the slug/path TEXT, the salt bytes, the salt path. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md:502:| `ledger_checkpoint_recorded` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `outcome` (str — CLOSED enum: `ledger_updated` / `ledger_missing` / `ledger_absent_from_plan` / `error` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape via the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator, else `unknown`; a path-traversal attempt smuggled through this field is rejected, not echoed), `scope_source` (str — CLOSED enum: `plan_dir` / `plan_ac` / `both` / `other`; how the commit was found to be in scope), `in_scope_path_count` (int 0..99 — clamped), `ledger_size_bucket_kib` (int 0..99 — clamped KiB bucket; the unit is in the field NAME), `over_ceiling` (int 0/1), `unverified_ac_claim_count` (int 0..99 — ledger bullets naming an AC/US id with no `verifier:` clause), `commits_since_last_observation` (int 0..99 — clamped), `state_kind` (str — CLOSED enum: `fresh` / `resumed` / `unavailable`; off-enum COERCED to `unavailable`), `would_block` (int 0/1 — what the FUTURE enforce flip WOULD have done; the hook has no deny path today), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W2 US6 / ADR-195 — the work-boundary ledger checkpoint, ADVISORY by construction (`check_ledger_checkpoint.py`, PreToolUse/Bash; no branch in that module returns `permissionDecision`). EVERY int is TYPE-strict: `bool` is rejected as an `int` subclass and a `float` becomes `0` rather than being rounded, because `_lib/canonical_json.py` refuses floats in HMAC-covered fields and the spool writer would drop the ENTIRE event to an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb (S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the commit MESSAGE, the committed PATHS, the ledger CONTENT, the repo root, any AC text. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md:503:| `ledger_checkpoint_skipped` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `reason` (str — CLOSED enum: `out_of_scope_paths` / `kill_switch` / `hotfix` / `exploratory` / `operator_opt_out` / `unparseable` / `budget_exhausted` / `no_repo` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed — the reason is an ENUM and never free text, so "why the rail stayed quiet" is countable without ever describing the commit), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN`, else `unknown`), `commits_since_last_observation` (int 0..99 — clamped), `state_kind` (str — CLOSED enum: `fresh` / `resumed` / `unavailable`), `would_block` (int 0/1 — always `0` on this row: a skip is never a would-block), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W2 US6 / ADR-195 — the same rail's NEGATIVE case, a separate action on purpose: the measure-first window needs a DENOMINATOR, and "skipped because the commit touched no plan-scoped path" and "never observed at all" are different facts that absence alone cannot distinguish. `reason=kill_switch` is emitted even when `CEO_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT=0`, so "the rail is off" is itself measured; `CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1` is the one fully silent posture (master precedence, CLAUDE.md §4). Same TYPE-strict int discipline as the row above. Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIPPED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. NO ATLAS technique. |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md:504:| `ledger_entry_rejected` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `signal` (str — fixed vocabulary of ONE: `ledger_write_gate`; this action has exactly one producer, so any other value names a caller that is not the gate and is COERCED), `decision` (str — CLOSED enum: `accept` / `reject`; an unreadable value COERCES to `reject`, FAIL-CLOSED, because an unreadable security verdict is a rejection and never an acceptance), `reason` (str — CLOSED enum: `ok` / `not_scanned_trusted_provenance` / `scanner_hit` / `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input`; off-enum COERCES to `malformed_input`, also fail-CLOSED), `family` (str — CLOSED enum, the UNION of the gate's own local families {`none`, `scanner_unavailable`, `oversize`, `malformed_input`, `unknown_family`} and the pattern CATALOGUE `_lib/injection_patterns.family_names()` {`directive_prose`, `harness_mimicry`, `provider_tokens`, `role_preamble`}; off-enum COERCED to `unknown_family`. Deliberately STRICTER than `prompt_injection_detected`, whose branch allowlists `family` by NAME but leaves its VALUE caller-chosen), `hits_count` (int 0..9999 — clamped), `bytes_scanned` (int 0..8192 — clamped at the gate's `MAX_ENTRY_BYTES`; an oversize body is rejected WITHOUT scanning, so this ceiling can never truncate a legitimate value), `scanned` (int 0/1), `enforced` (int 0/1 — whether the fail-CLOSED verdict BINDS in the current posture; kept separate from `decision` so an advisory-window row records what enforcement WOULD have done without pretending it happened), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W4 / ADR-195 — the ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), registered by Owner decision 2026-08-25 ("3 actions"). It exists precisely so a discard is NOT filed as `prompt_injection_detected`: routing `scanner_unavailable` / `oversize` / `malformed_input` into a DETECTION action would poison the very false-positive series the advisory window has to measure. There is deliberately NO fallback action — a missing or raising emitter degrades to a LOUD breadcrumb and `audit_channel="unavailable"`, never to a quieter series. Typed emitter `emit_ledger_entry_rejected` (keywords mirror `GateVerdict.to_audit_fields()` exactly). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the rejected entry BODY (not even a truncated preview — public repo, LLM06), the entry id, and any path. NO ATLAS technique (the DETECTION that may underlie a `scanner_hit` is `prompt_injection_detected`'s job; this row is the gate's disposal record). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md-505-| `env_var_hijack_blocked` (v2.41) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `hijack_class` (str — CLOSED enum: `linker_preload` / `linker_path` / `runtime_hook` / `linker_other` / `parse_failure`; unrecognized value COERCED to `parse_failure`, never echoed), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_in`/`tokens_out`/`tokens_total`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-133 A1 (Goose-harvest) — env-var hijack guard breadcrumb (`LD_PRELOAD`/`DYLD_*`/`LD_LIBRARY_PATH` and kin blocked on Bash). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_ENV_VAR_HIJACK_BLOCKED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the var name, the value, the command bytes. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
